THE RADICAL PAIR MECHANISM — The quantum core of the dipole effect

Hundreds of studies have found that weak magnetic fields can significantly influence various biological systems. However, the magnetic energies implicated in these effects are much smaller than thermal energies. The radical pair mechanism involves the quantum dynamics of the electron and nuclear spins of transient radical molecules.
