Here is how it works at the atomic level: When radiation hits a cell and generates two radicals simultaneously from the same molecule, those radicals are born as a correlated pair — their electron spins are entangled in either a singlet state (spins opposite) or triplet state (spins parallel). The singlet and triplet states have different chemical reactivity:

